    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Range of a Transformed Reciprocal Function",
    "problem": "What is the range of $f(x)=-\\frac{3}{5-2x}-2?$",
    "worked_solution": "A transformed reciprocal function of the form\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{a}{bx+c}+d\n$$\n\nhas the horizontal asymptote $y=d,$ and therefore, its range is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,d)\\cup (d,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $d=-2.$ Therefore, the horizontal asymptote is $y=-2,$ and the range of the function is\n\n$$\nf(x)\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe graph $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13932118/assets/51bdabd83a57cce915c284a27699aa200712b259257c371d9e1f19a4b60fa790.png)",
