    "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-141144: touching and reversing at x=6 indicates even multiplicity greater than one. q-80303: crossing at -2 gives odd multiplicity; the flattened crossing at 1 gives odd multiplicity greater than one, so only II holds. q-38770: the crossing at 2 is simple, the touch at -1 has even multiplicity, and the right tail rises, so I and II hold. q-80348: the roots -1, 0, 2 have respective multiplicities 1, odd greater than one, odd greater than one, matching option 3. q-112596: roots -2 and 3 are simple and 0 has odd multiplicity greater than one, matching option 2. q-106736: the nonzero reciprocal term takes every nonzero real value, so the range excludes only -2. q-64676: -135 degrees is coterminal with 225 degrees, in quadrant III. q-113743: an antiderivative of 2/5 is (2/5)y+C. q-8258: the argument is pi-arctan(5/2), approximately 1.95130, rounding to 1.95. q-288825: Vieta's product is c/a=-391. q-5729: each of seven positions independently has 26+10=36 choices, giving 36^7. q-113826: multiplying by the reciprocal and canceling gives 18/(z+1), with the original quotient requiring z distinct from -1 and 2. q-41240: the logarithm covers all real outputs, and the nonzero vertical scaling and shift preserve that range. q-30055: (x-1)^2=1 gives p=-1, q=1, pq=-1, and roots 0 and 2 with sum 2. q-86404: (y+6)^2=20 gives p+q=26. q-92875: cubing the root equation gives 5x+12=27 and x=3. No earlier submitted answer or grade was supplied; confirmation rests on mathematical verification and the captured worked solutions.",
